      "id": 11,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Every container against its compose limit",
      "description": "One row per running K2 container. Limits are read from the container's cgroup, so a compose change shows here after `up`. CPU is the 2-minute average. Process memory / limit is the figure to watch: above 90% the container is close to an out-of-memory kill. File cache is reclaimable page cache the kernel drops under pressure, so a high value is normal for MinIO. Working set is RSS plus recently used cache. OOM kills counts kills since the container started: any value above 0 is a problem, but cAdvisor here has no /dev/kmsg, so 0 is not proof; `docker inspect` OOMKilled is. Click a header to sort.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 21,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
